<title>GREECE: Nederlanden, Alpha lead Greek growth funds in July.</title>
<headline>Nederlanden, Alpha lead Greek growth funds in July.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nationale Nederlanden and Alpha Growth mutual funds topped Greece's 27 growth funds in the seven months to July with returns of 69.92 and 58.96 percent respectively, the association of institutional investors said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Five funds outperformed the Athens bourse's benchmark index in the January-July period, down from eight a month earlier.</p>
<p>The Athens stock exchange's general index started the year at 954.54 and gained 643.8 points or 67.45 percent to 1,598.34 points in the seven months to July 31.</p>
<p>Growth fund assets under management reached 165.9 billion drachmas in end-July, up 122.21 percent since the beginning of the year and 5.51 percent on June.</p>
<p>Growth funds made up 3.08 percent of the mutual fund industry's total assets which rose to 5.68 trillion drachmas in end-July, an increase of 4.93 percent on June and 50.8 percent since the start of the year.</p>
